#question(title: [An equation for volumes by “cylindrical shells"])[
  Let $a < b$.

  Let $f$ be a continuous, positive function
  defined on $[a, b]$.

  Let $R$ be the region in the first quadrant
  bounded between the graph of $f$ and the
  $x$-axis.

  Find a formula for the volume of the solid
  of revolution obtained by rotation the
  region $R$ around the $y$-axis.
]
